    "title": "Community, environmental leaders meet at Credit Island, Davenport - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Linda Cook ,\n56 minutes ago\nCommunity and environmental leaders got together Thursday at Credit Island, Davenport, for a morning of learning and outdoor exploration.\nThe Bi-State Conservation Action Network hosted the \"Confluence\" event. It featured a keynote speech from Nahant Marsh Executive Director Brian Ritter, hands-on workshops and networking. Participants also explored how local environmental data can be turned into creative maps and artwork.\nOrganizers said the event is designed for anyone interested in creating environmental change.\n.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WHBF - OurQuadCities.com.",
